# ── REAL UTILITY DATA — NEVER COMMIT ────────────────────────────────
# "the results must remain private. NO LEAKING THE DATA."
# This repo has a public-facing GitHub remote and is destined for GitHub Pages.
# Verify before every commit:  git check-ignore -v testcasefull.csv
testcasefull.csv
*full.csv
/real/
**/real-data/
/tmp-data/

# Real exports stay local. The tracked exception is input/*.csv, which are
# ANONYMISED samples committed on purpose and used by test_samples.mjs; the
# unit tests otherwise build their own synthetic export in test_fixtures.mjs.
# A real study export dropped anywhere else shows up in `git status` and the
# check above is what catches it.
testcase.csv
Groupings.csv

# ── ARCHIVED EXPLORATION — untracked by design ──────────────────────
# The feasibility spike: benchmark harnesses, generators, raw result JSON,
# and the two superseded planning docs (orchestrate.md, spec.md).
# Everything worth keeping was distilled into docs/. See docs/benchmarks.md.
/archive/

# Build artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
.DS_Store

# parser/block.wasm is NOT ignored: D9 requires either a CI build step or a
# committed binary, and a Pages deploy without it fails at compileStreaming.
# public/block.wasm is the prebuild copy of that same file — generated, so
# ignored.
public/block.wasm
